.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LOGCMP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm logcmp
.Nd capability-mode structured logging component
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the base provider for
.Dq org.5bsd.log
version
.Dq 1.0.0 .
It runs only from
.Pa /Capabilities/System/LogCmp.cap .
Each global service connection creates an isolated worker and bounded
single-producer record ring.
The worker drains bursts on a bounded periodic
.Xr kqueue 2
timer, so record publication does not require a control message per record.
An explicit flush drains all records published before the request and submits
them to the syslog capability before replying.
This is a processing boundary, not a guarantee that syslogd has committed the
records to stable storage.
The worker enters capability mode and forwards validated records through a
separately limited
.Dq system.syslog
Casper channel.
.Pp
The provider adds the trusted service label, component instance, provider
sequence, and receive time at the sink.
Clients supply severity, message text, and bounded non-reserved fields.
Ring exhaustion is explicit and observable; it never overwrites unread
records.
.Sh SECURITY
Workers cannot open files, sockets, or other sinks.
They cannot fork or execute and neither the syslog capability nor ring
consumer descriptors can be transferred to the client.
The global provider remains outside consumer coalitions.
Session creation and rejected records are audited through OpenBSM.
Lifecycle, accepted-record, and drop paths expose DTrace probes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr liblogcmp 3 ,
.Xr libshmring 3 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr serviced 8 ,
.Xr syslogd 8
